# Frozen 2026-09-15, the pass that turned `run-lint-gates.sh --ratchets` on.
# Comment blocks over the 10-line limit that predate the gate. Owner directive
# (AGENTS.md priority 6): two lines at the point of use; longer text goes into
# docs/ with a pointer. Two-way, and SHRINKING one is how a row leaves: bring a
# block under the limit, then DELETE its line here.
# Format: <file>	<first comment line, truncated to 60 chars>.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md#comment-size-comment-size
#
# Nothing here is new debt: these are the file headers this repo writes on
# purpose - what a script is for, what it delegates upstream, and the measured
# reason a shape is what it is. Each is a candidate for a docs/ page with a
# pointer, and each such move is its own edit rather than a side effect of
# turning the ratchet on.

# FILE HEADERS. The block starts at the shebang, so the key is that line and the
